/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_37.wav|Vertin|en|What's this?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_38.wav|Vertin|en|What do you want?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_4.wav|Vertin|en|He looks remarkably similar to a friend of ours who was lost in the "Storm" in 1929.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_40.wav|Vertin|en|I'd be delighted to meet your friends.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_41.wav|Vertin|en|Thank you for the warning, and the map. Let's hope I won't find any occasion to use it.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_42.wav|Vertin|en|I'll speak with her and see what she thinks.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_43.wav|Vertin|en|Admiral, with you in charge here now, I thought I might ask a favor.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_44.wav|Vertin|en|My apologies, Lieutenant. Perhaps you could point us in the right direction?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_45.wav|Vertin|en|There are oil drums on board!
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_46.wav|Vertin|en|Have you found what you lost since we last met?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_47.wav|Vertin|en|I'm not entirely surprised. Intelligence suggests they are closely associated with the Apostles Brotherhood.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_48.wav|Vertin|en|Manus Vindictae?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_49.wav|Vertin|en|Your performance on the training ground earlier was most impressive, Ms. Lopera.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_5.wav|Vertin|en|Thank you.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_50.wav|Vertin|en|Oh! Sorry, Lilya. I haven't had the chance to speak with you privately. The Admiral asked if you could stay on site to help with training their new recruits.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_51.wav|Vertin|en|What do you think? You can do as you wish.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_52.wav|Vertin|en|It's you!
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_53.wav|Vertin|en|Ms. Barbara provided us with some information.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_54.wav|Vertin|en|Sotheby, do we have everything?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_55.wav|Vertin|en|Hm ...
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_56.wav|Vertin|en|So, the kitchen even prepares food for them.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_57.wav|Vertin|en|Hold your fire, Lopera!
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_6.wav|Vertin|en|Things may become quite complicated during our visit to São Paulo. I wonder if I might request Zeno spare some manpower to assist us.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_7.wav|Vertin|en|Lilya, I've told Admiral Igor that he can rely on you for further assistance as necessary. Is that alright with you?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_8.wav|Vertin|en|Is this the entrance?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part01_9.wav|Vertin|en|This ship is headed to São Paulo. Is that where you're heading as well? Would you like to accompany us?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_1.wav|Vertin|en|What makes you say so?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_11.wav|Vertin|en|Sorry to show up without proper notice.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_12.wav|Vertin|en|She ...
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_13.wav|Vertin|en|My map—have you seen it? I have to get to the Veterans' Residence. They may very well be waiting for me there.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_14.wav|Vertin|en|His name was Karson. Did Mr. Duncan ever go by that name?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_15.wav|Vertin|en|I remember we all fell into the water.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_16.wav|Vertin|en|He's given us three days.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_17.wav|Vertin|en|May I see Dr. Dores's room?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_18.wav|Vertin|en|Mamãe Mariana, could I have a word with you, please? I have some questions about Mr. Duncan.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_2.wav|Vertin|en|Dr. Dores is being held captive in the colonel's manor.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_20.wav|Vertin|en|I knew a gentleman who looked just like him.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_21.wav|Vertin|en|Still alive? What's the bad news, then?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_22.wav|Vertin|en|Thank goodness. You survived, too. What about Sotheby?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_23.wav|Vertin|en|But Lopera and Sotheby ... Where are they?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_24.wav|Vertin|en|Doctor?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_25.wav|Vertin|en|Hmm?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_26.wav|Vertin|en|I think ... Ms. Kimberly, didn't you pull me out of the water?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_27.wav|Vertin|en|Come along. Let's take a peek inside.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_28.wav|Vertin|en|These must be articles that she hasn't sent out yet.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_29.wav|Vertin|en|We've got bad news. Dr. Dores has been abducted by the Brotherhood.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_3.wav|Vertin|en|What?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_30.wav|Vertin|en|Shortly after my fever subsided, I started to remember what happened just before I lost consciousness.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_31.wav|Vertin|en|*cough*
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_32.wav|Vertin|en|Funny, I've never thought to open a door like that before.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_33.wav|Vertin|en|He says that if Zeno doesn't return the deserters they detained, he'll execute the doctor.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_34.wav|Vertin|en|A crow?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_35.wav|Vertin|en|Just a little while.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_36.wav|Vertin|en|Do you have any photos of him?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_37.wav|Vertin|en|Hmm?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_38.wav|Vertin|en|Santos.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_39.wav|Vertin|en|Do you see any drafts? Any samples?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_40.wav|Vertin|en|There was a voice ringing in my head. It was you calling out to me, "Vertin, I can't have you dying here! You mustn't give up!"
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_42.wav|Vertin|en|Mamãe Mariana, please contact Admiral Igor. We need Zeno's help.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_43.wav|Vertin|en|That's a shame. I was looking forward to meeting them. Hopefully we'll see them soon.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_5.wav|Vertin|en|How long ago did Mr. Duncan move here? Do you remember?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_6.wav|Vertin|en|Do be careful, Ms. Kimberly.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_7.wav|Vertin|en|Where am I?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_8.wav|Vertin|en|No, no, it wasn't a bad joke at all, really.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part02_9.wav|Vertin|en|We'll bring her home safely.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_1.wav|Vertin|en|Admiral Igor has sent reinforcements. We were instructed to await their arrival at this location.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_10.wav|Vertin|en|And enjoy your new life, Nala, starting today.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_11.wav|Vertin|en|More rebels came at us following the gunfire, and we were forced to flee the base.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_12.wav|Vertin|en|It's unfortunate that we have to meet again under these circumstances.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_13.wav|Vertin|en|Lopera, could you tell us what happened?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_14.wav|Vertin|en|We couldn't halt Igor's escape.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_15.wav|Vertin|en|No contract, no seal.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_16.wav|Vertin|en|If you've got nowhere else to go, you can come to the Foundation with me if you like.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_17.wav|Vertin|en|Come.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_19.wav|Vertin|en|It's been shattered into pieces. You're free, Kimberly. You don't have to take orders from anyone anymore.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_2.wav|Vertin|en|I'm here. It's okay. You're going to be alright.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_20.wav|Vertin|en|I'll let them know you risked your life to protect me from the Zeno rebels. Anyway, the choice is yours.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_21.wav|Vertin|en|If Lopera's also joined the rebellion ...
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_22.wav|Vertin|en|White Rum, could you take us to the Zeno base?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_23.wav|Vertin|en|We'll come back for you later.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_24.wav|Vertin|en|The wind-up toy's been destroyed.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_25.wav|Vertin|en|Do you know him?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_26.wav|Vertin|en|I wasn't informed of this. What does she have to do with Zeno?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_27.wav|Vertin|en|Are we setting off now, Commander Ptolemy?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_28.wav|Vertin|en|"A report from Colombia: The mugshots of Pablo Emilio Escobar Gaviria do not match those archived. Similar anomalies have appeared for other notable figures."
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_29.wav|Vertin|en|Don't. He's not going to give it back to you.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_3.wav|Vertin|en|Ms. Moldir.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_31.wav|Vertin|en|And why does he want Kimberly?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_32.wav|Vertin|en|Could it be that ...
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_33.wav|Vertin|en|No one can control you anymore. You belong to no master; only yourself.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_34.wav|Vertin|en|Why did Igor abduct Ms. Urd?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_35.wav|Vertin|en|Oh, so the captive in that tower was Ms. Kimberly?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_36.wav|Vertin|en|Yes. But you should stay here. Igor still wants you.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_37.wav|Vertin|en|Yes, whatever you want.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_38.wav|Vertin|en|Yes, no longer reliant on or under the control of anyone.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_4.wav|Vertin|en|Nala ...
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_40.wav|Vertin|en|London, Lima, Ushuaia ...
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_41.wav|Vertin|en|But why would Igor ...?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_42.wav|Vertin|en|What's the situation at their base?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_43.wav|Vertin|en|Then we go ourselves.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_44.wav|Vertin|en|Mr. Karson!
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_45.wav|Vertin|en|We failed.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_46.wav|Vertin|en|Just think about who you are, what you want.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_48.wav|Vertin|en|And where are Igor and his army going? Why did they defect?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_49.wav|Vertin|en|Or maybe there's more to it.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_5.wav|Vertin|en|The "Storm" doesn't kill people? At least, not physically?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_50.wav|Vertin|en|You're no longer bound by anyone.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_52.wav|Vertin|en|Mr. Karson, who was reversed by the "Storm" of 1929, has somehow reappeared in 1990.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_6.wav|Vertin|en|As far as I'm aware, the Zeno officer at Tuesday's Motel committed suicide. Kimberly had nothing to do with it.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_7.wav|Vertin|en|*pant*
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_8.wav|Vertin|en|Everything will be fine, Kimberly.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter8_part03_9.wav|Vertin|en|All I know is that she was sent to the colonel's manor earlier.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_1.wav|Vertin|en|No need to apologize. In fact, the person you just mentioned sounds like someone we're looking for.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_10.wav|Vertin|en|I'm the Timekeeper of the St. Pavlov Foundation.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_11.wav|Vertin|en|You're right. We need to get there as soon as we can.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_12.wav|Vertin|en|We appreciate your kind consideration, Ms. Jailer, but we still have some unfinished business here.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_13.wav|Vertin|en|I'd wager she's spoken to that gentleman. That is ... if she has been here at all.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_14.wav|Vertin|en|We'd love to. Umm, only if that's okay with you, Ms. Jailer?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_15.wav|Vertin|en|No. I'm looking for a blind woman. Her name is Dores.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_16.wav|Vertin|en|Hmm. She'd have arrived here about three days ago. It's also possible that she came as a visitor, not a prisoner.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_17.wav|Vertin|en|Do you know where she is now?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_18.wav|Vertin|en|Hard to say. But things have been suspiciously quiet these past few days.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_19.wav|Vertin|en|So you assume Aleph is a man.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_20.wav|Vertin|en|She used to be a doctor at the São Paulo Veterans' Residence in Brazil.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_21.wav|Vertin|en|This all sounds very complicated. When will your magazine be finished then?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_22.wav|Vertin|en|Careful and well-considered as ever, Sonetto. It's possible they've already infiltrated Ushuaia, just as they did in Chisos.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_23.wav|Vertin|en|Certainly.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_24.wav|Vertin|en|I think the person I'm looking for might have attended this literary salon, or at least talked to some of its members.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_25.wav|Vertin|en|And how much do you know about this pen pal of yours?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_26.wav|Vertin|en|Are you alright?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_27.wav|Vertin|en|My assistant and I are here to visit Comala Prison on official orders from the Foundation. Here, this is my ID.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_28.wav|Vertin|en|Could you tell me where you last saw her?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_29.wav|Vertin|en|She's a blind woman who always carries an old typewriter.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_3.wav|Vertin|en|I see. Thank you, Miss. Perhaps we made a mistake.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_30.wav|Vertin|en|We came here with different goals, and still, none of them have been accomplished.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_31.wav|Vertin|en|Don't worry. This isn't the first time we've ended up on the wrong side of the bars.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_32.wav|Vertin|en|Don't worry, Ms. Jailer. We made it out in one piece.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_33.wav|Vertin|en|Pardon?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_34.wav|Vertin|en|But the Zeno rebels may still be holding Dores. We can't just wait around. I'm afraid we'll have to take the risk.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_35.wav|Vertin|en|Then she was here.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_36.wav|Vertin|en|You have a pen pal ... in here?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_37.wav|Vertin|en|I had been hoping we'd find some clues here in Ushuaia after we lost track of the Manus in the "Free Breeze" shipwreck.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_38.wav|Vertin|en|For now, it seems our new friend's story lines up with the intel from Moth. It seems the Zeno rebels really did bring Dr. Dores here. We should see if there's anything more she can tell us.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_39.wav|Vertin|en|Did you understand what that man just said?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_4.wav|Vertin|en|Dores?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_40.wav|Vertin|en|She does have a point.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_41.wav|Vertin|en|These people seem friendly enough. Why don't we see what this is about?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_42.wav|Vertin|en|Though, this cell is quite different from the ones we've been in before.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_43.wav|Vertin|en|So, she's a writer, too.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_44.wav|Vertin|en|Ms. Jailer, is this that peculiarity about Comala you mentioned earlier?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_45.wav|Vertin|en|I see. No wonder Ms. Recoleta has gone to such lengths to become a part of it.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_46.wav|Vertin|en|Thank you for inviting me here, Mr. Idealist.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_47.wav|Vertin|en|Don't worry, Sonetto. I would guess we're not the only ones who are confused here.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_48.wav|Vertin|en|What's your business there, if you don't mind our asking?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_49.wav|Vertin|en|Sorry to interrupt, but did you just say "official credentials"?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_5.wav|Vertin|en|I have a strange feeling about it all. They're definitely up to something.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_50.wav|Vertin|en|I agree. Let's see if we can talk to some of the inmates and find out what they know.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_51.wav|Vertin|en|It seems he had a mental breakdown and lost control of his arcane skill. It appears that every line he recited carried unbridled power.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_52.wav|Vertin|en|When did all of this happen?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_53.wav|Vertin|en|Ms. Recoleta, you've gone to great lengths to get into the Panopticon. Would you mind telling us why?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_54.wav|Vertin|en|Ms. Jailer, do you mean ...
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_55.wav|Vertin|en|Ms. Recoleta, I'm Vertin, and this is Sonetto. We're investigators from the St. Pavlov Foundation.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_56.wav|Vertin|en|Correct. Is there anything more you could tell us about the day you met her?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_57.wav|Vertin|en|Forgive me, but I'm not sure what a floating sheep, a jarring reading experience, and all this constant rewriting are meant to express.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_58.wav|Vertin|en|They would've gone to ground, somewhere remote and off the radar. Indeed, it's possible they've already left Ushuaia.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_59.wav|Vertin|en|We appreciate your help, Ms. ...
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_6.wav|Vertin|en|I have some questions for the gentleman as well, but we're more than willing to follow the rules.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_60.wav|Vertin|en|Actually, my assistant and I are here to inquire about a prisoner named Dores. Does that name sound familiar?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_61.wav|Vertin|en|Hold on. I've been meaning to ask—why are you only calling her "Jailer"?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_62.wav|Vertin|en|And on the subject of different names, she once wrote for UTTU under the name "Urd."
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_63.wav|Vertin|en|Don't you know her name? Or do you just prefer addressing people by their occupation?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_64.wav|Vertin|en|For whatever reason, it seems they haven't been pushing for the "Storm" to happen quite as eagerly as before.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_65.wav|Vertin|en|Please get down, Ms. Recoleta. Someone's coming our way.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_7.wav|Vertin|en|Ushuaia's not very big. If Manus Vindictae is here, we'll notice. Stay sharp.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_8.wav|Vertin|en|Isn't that the prologue writer?!
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part01_9.wav|Vertin|en|Who is that?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_10.wav|Vertin|en|Please, calm yourself, Ms. Recoleta.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_11.wav|Vertin|en|"By becoming the Panopticon's sole patron, they seized control of the resources and the allocation system, turning this place into a living hell. I suspect that the Physician, the current highest authority here, is responsible for this situation."
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_12.wav|Vertin|en|The jailer told me she went back to the gallery once everything calmed down.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_13.wav|Vertin|en|Including the roll results of the "absolutely random" Die.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_14.wav|Vertin|en|Yes, that's right. Do you know her? You're the first person I've met here to speak plainly about her.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_15.wav|Vertin|en|If she's leading us astray on purpose, why? Ms. Recoleta, what do you think? Could she be Aleph?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_16.wav|Vertin|en|How can we help you?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_17.wav|Vertin|en|Spontaneous order?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_18.wav|Vertin|en|Sorry. What exactly is your story about?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_19.wav|Vertin|en|Ms. Recoleta, this is all in your novel, isn't it?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_2.wav|Vertin|en|What if we present you with stronger evidence to prove it's more than just a coincidence?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_20.wav|Vertin|en|Oh, I see. I must've missed that. Sorry. Still, it's a beautiful story. Sad, but beautiful.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_21.wav|Vertin|en|I ... I wonder if the protagonist ever finds this "Die of Babylon" in the end.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_22.wav|Vertin|en|Is that all?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_23.wav|Vertin|en|Are you suggesting that someone is controlling the Panopticon in order to make it follow the same plot as your story?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_24.wav|Vertin|en|Then it seems only the Physician knows the whereabouts of Dr. Dores. Ms. Jailer, we need to meet with the Physician. It's important.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_25.wav|Vertin|en|Well, according to the Idealist and our jailer, any inmates who are unwell will be taken to the Physician.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_26.wav|Vertin|en|Wait. Are you saying that everyone we've met here matches a character from your story, like some kind of archetype?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_27.wav|Vertin|en|Understood.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_28.wav|Vertin|en|That's terribly kind of you. But honestly, I think we've had enough poetry today to last a lifetime.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_29.wav|Vertin|en|Perhaps we all need to start writing our own stories.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_3.wav|Vertin|en|By process of elimination, it's almost certain that your pen pal, Aleph, is right behind this door.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_30.wav|Vertin|en|Thank you for your assistance, Ms. Recoleta. Without your precise predictions, we wouldn't be standing here now.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_31.wav|Vertin|en|She found nothing: no blood, no shell cases, not even a trace of the Idealist.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_32.wav|Vertin|en|"... I discovered that the inmates were put through brutal training, even when they were too sick to carry out their tasks. They also forced pure-blood arcanist inmates to wear their masks, effectively turning them into murmuring puppets ..."
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_33.wav|Vertin|en|Please.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_34.wav|Vertin|en|If that's true, Ms. Recoleta, it's very likely that the one acting against us is in fact Aleph himself.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_35.wav|Vertin|en|Ms. Recoleta said the Panopticon could collapse because of the Die of Babylon.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_36.wav|Vertin|en|What if they're not just fantasies? What if they're tied to the very survival of this place?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_37.wav|Vertin|en|"The Physician told me the horrifying truth about the Panopticon of Comala and the power behind it—Manus Vindictae."
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_38.wav|Vertin|en|It's unlikely that the jailer will let us search the central tower, even in this situation. We should take the initiative and look for clues while she's away.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_39.wav|Vertin|en|We need to speak to this Physician first.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_4.wav|Vertin|en|That they've set the rules, started the poetry group, planned the attack on the Idealist, and tried to prevent us from finding Dr. Dores?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_41.wav|Vertin|en|The jailer has already confirmed that she wasn't the one to fire at the Idealist. The shot came from somewhere else in the room.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_42.wav|Vertin|en|That sounds unbelievable. But, then again, maybe you're onto something.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_43.wav|Vertin|en|Please, calm down, Ms. Recoleta. I think she's telling the truth.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_44.wav|Vertin|en|Couldn't you make an exception?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_45.wav|Vertin|en|It's possible someone brought him there while everyone else was shouting and running about.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_46.wav|Vertin|en|This is all just speculation. If we want to find the Idealist or Dr. Dores ...
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_47.wav|Vertin|en|I remember.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_48.wav|Vertin|en|If everything in the Panopticon proceeds according to Ms. Recoleta's novel, as she says, she should be able to predict what happens next.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_49.wav|Vertin|en|Ms. Octavia. I hope you've come with something more important to share than just some criticism of the Idealist.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_5.wav|Vertin|en|There's nothing that we can be certain of for now. But on a brighter note, we didn't come back empty-handed from our mission either, Sonetto.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_50.wav|Vertin|en|Come out, now. Whoever's out there, speak up.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_51.wav|Vertin|en|Ms. Octavia, please continue the congress, and let the next inmate perform their roll. Then Ms. Recoleta's statement will be proven true.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_52.wav|Vertin|en|Ms. Octavia, what brings you here at this hour?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_53.wav|Vertin|en|To be fair, the gunshot was quite loud, as was the ensuing commotion.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_54.wav|Vertin|en|It worked, didn't it?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_55.wav|Vertin|en|Do you know where she might be?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_56.wav|Vertin|en|To be honest, Ms. Recoleta. I wasn't sure you'd be able to correctly predict everything.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_57.wav|Vertin|en|Ms. Recoleta, do you believe that the Idealist could be your pen pal, Aleph?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_58.wav|Vertin|en|You see the world through a different lens that none of us share.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_59.wav|Vertin|en|I haven't yet grasped the connection between the Die, your novel, and what's happening in this place, but ...
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_6.wav|Vertin|en|This way, you can prove to Ms. Jailer the irrefutable connection between Comala and your novel, The Rise and Fall of Sanity.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_60.wav|Vertin|en|We're no strangers to wild guesses, and sometimes they're closer to the truth than you'd think. So this ...
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_61.wav|Vertin|en|Are you alright? You don't seem as excited as when we first entered Comala.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_62.wav|Vertin|en|We found Dr. Dores's signature in the gallery. You were right all along, Recoleta. She was here.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_63.wav|Vertin|en|The Physician again. Everything eventually leads back to him, just as we suspected.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_64.wav|Vertin|en|Now's our chance, Sonetto.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_65.wav|Vertin|en|Maybe. But the handwriting in that notebook is most certainly Urd's.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_66.wav|Vertin|en|Just as Ms. Recoleta predicted.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_7.wav|Vertin|en|Ms. Recoleta, please make your prediction for the next inmate's die roll.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_8.wav|Vertin|en|I suggest we focus on our respective missions instead of fighting with one another.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part02_9.wav|Vertin|en|No one would've thought to come looking for them here.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_1.wav|Vertin|en|Mr. García, do you need a hand?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_10.wav|Vertin|en|Of course not. We still have questions he needs to answer.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_11.wav|Vertin|en|But the Manus ritual ...
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_12.wav|Vertin|en|This room's about to collapse. We've got to leave.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_13.wav|Vertin|en|A day when both the clouds and sun were visible? Could you be more specific?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_14.wav|Vertin|en|*cough* Yes, and you? And Ms. Recoleta, are you okay?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_15.wav|Vertin|en|"They"?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_16.wav|Vertin|en|Still, I wonder what your relationship is with him.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_17.wav|Vertin|en|An era?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_18.wav|Vertin|en|I see. Mr. Aleph, members of the Foundation branch will arrive soon to evaluate your condition. I hope you'll answer their questions with the same patience you showed us. Thank you.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_19.wav|Vertin|en|Okay. I trust you.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_2.wav|Vertin|en|"Dear Mr. Aleph, my apologies if this reaches you at an inconvenient time. I am Dores, pen name 'Urd,' an ordinary inmate of the Panopticon of Comala. I write seeking your guidance, if you wouldn't mind offering it to me."
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_20.wav|Vertin|en|Could you lend it to us? The situation's urgent, Mr. Aleph.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_21.wav|Vertin|en|I think I understand now. The Idealist and the Physician are both parts of you, or, to put it another way, they're your alter egos.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_22.wav|Vertin|en|Stay vigilant, everyone. This is just like when the Idealist and the Physician had their meltdown.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_23.wav|Vertin|en|"Dear Mr. Aleph,"
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_24.wav|Vertin|en|So, sir, are you Aleph, the ruler of this prison?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_25.wav|Vertin|en|These letters we found have answered a great deal, but there's still something that isn't clear.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_26.wav|Vertin|en|Not until you get your "answer."
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_27.wav|Vertin|en|Perhaps not every question needs an answer, Mr. Aleph.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_28.wav|Vertin|en|"Why are you so interested in the Panopticon of Comala?"
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_29.wav|Vertin|en|So you're saying that, to you, we're no different from Manus Vindictae?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_3.wav|Vertin|en|Dr. Dores, a guest of Manus Vindictae?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_30.wav|Vertin|en|Dr. Merlin, you keep mentioning "time." What exactly do you mean by that?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_31.wav|Vertin|en|You're not going to stop, are you?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_32.wav|Vertin|en|Take care of yourself, Recoleta.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_33.wav|Vertin|en|Mr. Aleph, when did Dr. Dores depart?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_34.wav|Vertin|en|Are you the one controlling the Panopticon with a die? The one hiding Ms. Dores's whereabouts?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_35.wav|Vertin|en|It seems we've stumbled upon the Physician's—
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_36.wav|Vertin|en|Recoleta ...
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_37.wav|Vertin|en|I'm not sure, but it could be bad. Come on. Let's go in and see if they're alright.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_38.wav|Vertin|en|Only this time, it seems even worse.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_39.wav|Vertin|en|Then I'd like to be the first to read this new novel, if that's alright?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_4.wav|Vertin|en|Aleph seems to be in a terrible state. We have to be careful. Something isn't right about that die!
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_40.wav|Vertin|en|Mr. Aleph, do you know anything about Manus Vindictae's ritual? How far has it progressed?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_41.wav|Vertin|en|What's happening?
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_42.wav|Vertin|en|Looks like Dores and Aleph are acquaintances. Or, at least, they've had some correspondence.
/data/admin4/dataset/hero5043/WAV/plotvoc_hero5043chapter9_part03_43.wav|Vertin|en|Mr. Aleph, what exactly did the Manus promise Dr. Dores?
